^ Math function examples demonstrating min, max, absolute, and round

^ Minimum of two numbers
LET the variable minval BE the minimum of the number 5 and the number 10
PROCLAIM the number minval

LET the variable minval2 BE the minimum of the number -3 and the number 7
PROCLAIM the number minval2

^ Maximum of two numbers
LET the variable maxval BE the maximum of the number 5 and the number 10
PROCLAIM the number maxval

LET the variable maxval2 BE the maximum of the number -3 and the number 7
PROCLAIM the number maxval2

^ Absolute value
LET the variable absval BE the absolute value of the number -42
PROCLAIM the number absval

LET the variable absval2 BE the absolute value of the number 42
PROCLAIM the number absval2

^ Round a number
LET the variable rounded BE the rounded value of the number 3.7
PROCLAIM the number rounded

LET the variable rounded2 BE the rounded value of the number 2.3
PROCLAIM the number rounded2

^ Using with variables
LET the variable a BE the number 15
LET the variable b BE the number 25
LET the variable result BE the maximum of the value of a and the value of b
PROCLAIM the number result
